For each function the diff changes, find its callers (Grep for the symbol) and
check whether the change breaks any call site: a new precondition, a changed
return shape, a new exception, a timing/ordering dependency. Also check callees:
does a parallel change in the same PR make a call unsafe?
`,_Sz,Q5q,g5q="Cleanup and altitude candidates use the same `file`/`line`/`summary` shape; in\n`failure_scenario`, state the concrete cost (what is duplicated, wasted, or\nharder to maintain) instead of a crash. Correctness bugs always outrank\ncleanup and altitude findings when the output cap forces a cut.\n",UM9,zSz,ASz=`## Phase 3 \u2014 Sweep for gaps

